<library>
<description>Vishay VEML7700-TR ambient light sensor, LCSC C504893.

Land pattern and pin numbering from the EasyEDA library for C504893.
Package LED-SMD_4P, body 6.8 x 2.4 mm, four flat pads at 1.27 mm pitch,
0.80 x 1.80 mm. Nothing hidden under the body.

  1 SCL   2 VDD   3 GND   4 SDA

Note pin 1 and pin 4 are at OPPOSITE ends of the part, so SCL and SDA
approach from either side - worth knowing before routing.

I2C address is 0x10, fixed. Clear on this board: the bus already carries
0x3E (LCD), 0x60 (PCA9633 backlight), 0x62 (SCD41) and 0x68 (DS3231).
Supply 2.5-3.6 V, 16-bit, 0 to 120 klx, resolution down to ~0.0036 lx.

Chosen over the BH1750 (C78960, cheaper, more stock) because low-light range
is the whole job here: the BH1750 bottoms out near 0.5-1 lx and a dark bedroom
IS 0.1-1 lx, so the decision would be made on noise.

Placement: the front face is fine - what matters is the light PATH, not the
face. Give it a light-tight collar from the board to the front panel so it only
ever sees through its own 3-4 mm aperture, and put it in a corner away from the
digits and the ring. See ../../docs/pcb-assembly.md.</description>
